261
00:22:00,646 --> 00:22:02,564
It was going pretty well.

262
00:22:04,066 --> 00:22:06,652
What do girls like so much
about that guy, Lee Chan, anyway?

263
00:22:06,735 --> 00:22:08,529
He used to be nothing
but an outcast and a loser.

264
00:22:09,738 --> 00:22:11,657
He used to be nothing
but an outcast and a loser.

265
00:22:11,740 --> 00:22:15,994
An outcast and a loser.

266
00:22:18,038 --> 00:22:19,248
"Outcast"?

267
00:22:21,333 --> 00:22:22,751
"Loser"?

268
00:22:26,588 --> 00:22:28,966
There she goes again.
Let's go stop her.

269
00:22:35,472 --> 00:22:38,392
I bet
people can't even imagine his past.

270
00:22:48,610 --> 00:22:50,487
- Was it you?
- Excuse me?

271
00:22:50,571 --> 00:22:53,657
You were the one bullying
and isolating him

272
00:22:54,283 --> 00:22:55,284
weren't you?

273
00:22:55,826 --> 00:23:00,497
I'm never going to forgive you!

274
00:23:21,602 --> 00:23:22,728
Your nose is bleeding.

275
00:23:27,316 --> 00:23:28,734
We're sorry.

276
00:23:29,484 --> 00:23:30,652
We're so sorry.

277
00:23:31,403 --> 00:23:34,531
My friend has been having
such a hard time finding a job

278
00:23:34,948 --> 00:23:37,034
- and life has been so rough
- You did well.

279
00:23:37,117 --> 00:23:39,578
that she ended up developing
anger management issues.

280
00:23:39,661 --> 00:23:41,330
We're truly sorry.

281
00:23:41,413 --> 00:23:42,998
We're so, truly sorry.

282
00:23:43,248 --> 00:23:46,209
What are you apologizing for?
I'm not sorry at all.

283
00:23:47,085 --> 00:23:49,504
Bullying is the worst.

284
00:23:50,088 --> 00:23:52,257
Do you even know what that's like?

285
00:23:58,138 --> 00:23:59,389
I'm sorry.

286
00:24:00,432 --> 00:24:02,643
You don't, do you?

287
00:24:15,656 --> 00:24:16,698
- Jeez.
- What are they doing?

288
00:24:17,115 --> 00:24:18,200
- What the...
- Did he hit her?

289
00:24:30,879 --> 00:24:35,842
My friend is so deeply apologetic
that she's on her knees.

290
00:24:35,926 --> 00:24:37,761
I guess she's reflecting
on her actions a lot, right?

291
00:24:38,345 --> 00:24:39,471
Right?

292
00:24:41,598 --> 00:24:42,641
Well...

293
00:24:43,517 --> 00:24:44,768
That's enough. Just leave.

294
00:24:45,477 --> 00:24:47,187
How generous of you.

295
00:24:47,270 --> 00:24:49,064
Bless you. Thank you.

296
00:24:49,147 --> 00:24:50,565
Thank you.

297
00:24:51,400 --> 00:24:52,484
Bye.

298
00:24:52,567 --> 00:24:54,945
Right?

299
00:24:55,195 --> 00:24:57,656
- Hey, let go of me!
- Knock it off.

300
00:24:57,990 --> 00:24:59,032
What?

301
00:24:59,491 --> 00:25:01,618
She got anger management issues
because she couldn't get a job?

302
00:25:03,203 --> 00:25:04,538
For someone who works at SE.

303
00:25:04,913 --> 00:25:06,039
Do you know her?

304
00:25:08,333 --> 00:25:09,543
She's a stranger.

305
00:25:10,293 --> 00:25:11,294
Exactly.

306
00:25:12,087 --> 00:25:13,255
I should've asked for her number.

307
00:25:14,172 --> 00:25:15,215
Hurry up.

308
00:25:16,299 --> 00:25:17,384
Jeez, wait.

309
00:25:19,636 --> 00:25:20,804
- Throw her.
- Throw her.

310
00:25:25,434 --> 00:25:26,560
Oh, man.

311
00:25:26,977 --> 00:25:28,020
It's like

312
00:25:28,186 --> 00:25:30,439
her weight literally doubled
the second she got drunk.

313
00:25:30,522 --> 00:25:31,606
Darn it.

314
00:25:35,444 --> 00:25:36,903
This is nuts.

315
00:25:38,405 --> 00:25:40,073
FOREVER LEE CHAN

316
00:25:40,157 --> 00:25:43,160
Goodness. Anyway,
I guess Da-reum really is

317
00:25:43,493 --> 00:25:45,746
living out the ultimate
successful fan.

318
00:25:47,122 --> 00:25:48,498
I wonder if Chan even knows

319
00:25:49,082 --> 00:25:50,959
that he still has such a die-hard fan

320
00:25:51,043 --> 00:25:52,919
when D.N.X disbanded a decade ago.

321
00:25:54,087 --> 00:25:55,130
Beats me.

322
00:25:56,339 --> 00:25:58,508
Hey, let's go home.

323
00:26:00,719 --> 00:26:01,970
Oh, wait.

324
00:26:05,474 --> 00:26:06,600
Come on, let's go.

325
00:26:55,148 --> 00:26:57,275
SUNGJU STATION

326
00:27:02,989 --> 00:27:04,116
SUNGJU STATION

327
00:27:51,079 --> 00:27:53,582
Which department are you in?

328
00:27:53,665 --> 00:27:55,709
I'm with the Merchandising Team.

329
00:27:56,585 --> 00:27:58,253
I'm in Marketing.

330
00:27:58,336 --> 00:27:59,838
Marketing? Me too.

331
00:27:59,921 --> 00:28:02,174
- Really?
- I hope we get along.

332
00:28:02,257 --> 00:28:04,134
My name is Park Young-woo.

333
00:28:04,217 --> 00:28:05,302
What are your names?

334
00:28:05,385 --> 00:28:08,180
My name is Lee Min-a.

335
00:28:08,263 --> 00:28:09,347
- Lee Min-a.
- Lee Min-a.

336
00:28:09,431 --> 00:28:10,849
My name is Nam Da-reum.

337
00:28:10,932 --> 00:28:13,560
- Nam Da-reum. Lee Min-a and Da-reum.
- Nam Da-reum.

338
00:28:13,643 --> 00:28:14,895
I see.

339
00:28:16,146 --> 00:28:17,439
Let's get along.

340
00:28:17,731 --> 00:28:19,941
You know they say
loyalty to your batchmates is key.

341
00:28:20,025 --> 00:28:21,610
- How about a fist bump?
- Sure.

342
00:28:22,903 --> 00:28:24,446
You guys became close already?

343
00:28:27,282 --> 00:28:30,118
Congratulations
on joining the Appello family.

344
00:28:30,202 --> 00:28:31,870
I'm Kim Mi-young

345
00:28:32,120 --> 00:28:35,582
the Marketing Team Manager.
I'll be running today's orientation.

346
00:28:36,625 --> 00:28:38,668
Here are your employee ID cards.

347
00:28:39,961 --> 00:28:41,922
- Mr. Young-woo.
- Thank you.

348
00:28:42,005 --> 00:28:43,632
- Ms. Min-a.
- Thank you.

349
00:28:43,840 --> 00:28:45,217
And Ms. Da-reum.

350
00:28:47,802 --> 00:28:49,012
Thank you.

351
00:28:49,512 --> 00:28:52,182
Appello currently has 82 employees

352
00:28:52,265 --> 00:28:54,226
plus three new hires joining today.

353
00:28:54,309 --> 00:28:57,270
That means this ID card is basically
Chan's limited-edition merch

354
00:28:57,354 --> 00:29:00,065
with only 85 of them
in the whole world.

355
00:29:00,857 --> 00:29:03,526
It's even customized!

356
00:29:04,277 --> 00:29:07,697
All right, then. Let's dive
into the official company overview.

357
00:29:08,365 --> 00:29:09,532
- Shall we?
- Yes, ma'am.

358
00:29:09,616 --> 00:29:10,617
This way.

359
00:29:13,745 --> 00:29:15,497
- Come this way.
- Yes, ma'am.

360
00:29:23,046 --> 00:29:24,339
They come in different colors...

361
00:29:26,049 --> 00:29:27,300
Ms. Min-a.

362
00:29:29,302 --> 00:29:32,472
Most of Appello's partner brands
are centered online

363
00:29:32,555 --> 00:29:35,892
we host pop-up spaces on floor one
so they can meet customers in person.

364
00:29:35,976 --> 00:29:37,018
It's all right.

365
00:29:37,852 --> 00:29:40,188
We also offer spaces for our brands

366
00:29:40,272 --> 00:29:42,565
such as sewing rooms,
pattern rooms, and studios.

367
00:29:43,316 --> 00:29:46,319
As you can see,
our dress code is completely free.

368
00:29:46,403 --> 00:29:48,780
From tomorrow on, you can wear
a swimsuit, party clothes

369
00:29:48,863 --> 00:29:50,198
or anything that fits your style.

370
00:29:59,666 --> 00:30:02,419
This is the studio
for lookbook and campaign shoots.

371
00:30:03,044 --> 00:30:05,463
All of Appello's visual content is
basically born right here.

372
00:30:25,358 --> 00:30:26,401
NAM DA-REUM

373
00:30:26,901 --> 00:30:30,572
On the fourth floor, we have
Marketing and Merchandising Teams.

374
00:30:32,657 --> 00:30:34,534
Oh, and the CEO's Office.

375
00:30:38,246 --> 00:30:41,458
All right. For our final stop,
let's go meet the CEO.

376
00:30:41,541 --> 00:30:43,877
- What, right now?
- Yes.

377
00:30:59,059 --> 00:31:01,811
Hello, I'm the new hire, Nam Da-reum.

378
00:31:02,937 --> 00:31:03,980
Too cheesy.

379
00:31:07,275 --> 00:31:09,361
Nice to meet you. I'm Nam Da-reum.

380
00:31:09,444 --> 00:31:10,737
"I'm Nam Da-reum."

381
00:31:11,529 --> 00:31:12,739
You sound like a call center agent.

382
00:31:14,240 --> 00:31:15,575
Just act normal.

383
00:31:15,825 --> 00:31:17,202
And don't freeze up in front of Chan.

384
00:31:19,120 --> 00:31:20,705
Here, a secret weapon.

385
00:31:25,210 --> 00:31:27,379
Take this calming pill,
and it will help with your nerves.

386
00:31:28,713 --> 00:31:29,964
The calming pill.

387
00:31:45,980 --> 00:31:46,981
Mr. Kang.

388
00:31:48,608 --> 00:31:50,485
They are our new recruits.

389
00:31:56,866 --> 00:31:59,494
- It's nice to meet you.
- I'm new! I mean I'm Park Young-woo.

390
00:32:01,496 --> 00:32:02,539
It's nice to meet you.

391
00:32:02,622 --> 00:32:06,376
Hello, I'm the new hire, Lee Min-a.

392
00:32:16,261 --> 00:32:17,387
It's nice to meet you.

393
00:32:35,655 --> 00:32:38,366
Is that you, Chan?

394
00:32:45,957 --> 00:32:48,960
What the? Why is it someone else?

395
00:32:53,381 --> 00:32:54,799
I'm Nam Da-reum.

396
00:32:55,967 --> 00:32:57,260
NAM DA-REUM

397
00:33:01,556 --> 00:33:03,558
Welcome to Appello.

398
00:33:03,641 --> 00:33:06,478
My door is always open,
so feel free to drop by anytime.

399
00:33:07,145 --> 00:33:09,731
Don't feel too intimidated,
and just treat me as a coworker.

400
00:33:10,648 --> 00:33:12,484
Let's do some great work together.

401
00:33:13,026 --> 00:33:14,068
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

402
00:33:14,819 --> 00:33:17,197
All right. Shall we wrap up here
and head out?

403
00:33:17,530 --> 00:33:19,532
- Thank you.
- Goodbye.

404
00:33:26,498 --> 00:33:27,707
It's Chan.

405
00:33:43,556 --> 00:33:44,682
Ms. Nam.

406
00:33:50,522 --> 00:33:51,898
Ms. Da-reum? What's wrong?

407
00:33:51,981 --> 00:33:54,651
- Are you okay? Try to breathe.
- Ms. Da-reum.

408
00:33:54,859 --> 00:33:56,319
- Please call 911.
- Breathe.

409
00:33:56,402 --> 00:33:58,071
- What is it?
- Is something stuck in her throat?

410
00:33:58,154 --> 00:33:59,864
- You can't breathe?
- What's wrong?

411
00:33:59,948 --> 00:34:00,990
- Goodness.
- Breathe.

412
00:34:01,115 --> 00:34:02,575
Try to breathe.

413
00:34:36,693 --> 00:34:37,735
Da-reum...

414
00:34:38,403 --> 00:34:39,696
Are you okay?

415
00:34:40,238 --> 00:34:41,447
She should be fine now.

416
00:34:42,365 --> 00:34:43,408
I'm not sure
what was choking her, though.

417
00:34:45,952 --> 00:34:47,036
- What...
- What's that?

418
00:34:47,120 --> 00:34:48,204
What is this?

419
00:35:09,267 --> 00:35:10,393
Oh, what's up?

420
00:35:10,727 --> 00:35:12,562
Listen up, everyone.
I've got big news.

421
00:35:12,645 --> 00:35:13,813
Did you guys hear?

422
00:35:13,896 --> 00:35:17,275
A new recruit named Nam Da-reum
made big trouble from day one.

423
00:35:18,192 --> 00:35:20,361
I mean, where is the discipline
in new recruits these days?

424
00:35:22,739 --> 00:35:23,781
What?

425
00:35:29,245 --> 00:35:30,705
Mr. Lee Jin-sang.

426
00:35:34,751 --> 00:35:35,835
Oops.

427
00:35:36,502 --> 00:35:37,503
My mistake.

428
00:35:40,632 --> 00:35:41,633
Go on.

429
00:35:45,970 --> 00:35:48,890
I threw up on Director Lee's pants
at my first company dinner.

430
00:35:51,893 --> 00:35:54,145
Anyone can make a mistake
when they're nervous.

431
00:35:54,646 --> 00:35:55,897
Don't worry about it.

432
00:35:58,066 --> 00:36:00,818
Thank you, Ms. Kim.

433
00:36:03,821 --> 00:36:06,115
Excuse me.

434
00:36:06,699 --> 00:36:10,453
But wasn't Mr. Lee Chan the CEO?

435
00:36:10,953 --> 00:36:13,456
The two were previously co-CEOs

436
00:36:13,539 --> 00:36:15,917
but recently, the system changed
and we now have one CEO.

437
00:36:16,793 --> 00:36:19,837
- Then...
- Director Lee is only in charge

438
00:36:19,921 --> 00:36:21,589
of the fashion
for Appello's key events.

439
00:36:25,301 --> 00:36:26,594
I see.

440
00:36:38,481 --> 00:36:40,066
What was it like
to finally see him in person?

441
00:36:40,149 --> 00:36:41,317
Did you manage to stay composed?

442
00:36:42,026 --> 00:36:45,405
A tear emoji? You must've cried.
Were you that moved?

443
00:36:45,488 --> 00:36:47,490
Let's throw a party
to remember your "made-it" moment.

444
00:36:47,573 --> 00:36:49,200
- What do you want to eat?
- I'm in!

445
00:36:49,283 --> 00:36:51,160
Let's eat
whatever Namda wants to eat today.

446
00:36:51,244 --> 00:36:52,578
- I'm in!
- I'm in!

447
00:36:52,662 --> 00:36:54,122
- We're in!
- We're in!

448
00:36:55,540 --> 00:36:58,668
Girls, this is Chan's company

449
00:36:59,085 --> 00:37:00,795
but he's not around.

450
00:37:02,088 --> 00:37:04,090
That's like saying
there are no pads in push-up bras.

451
00:37:04,173 --> 00:37:05,842
That one has 4cm pads.

452
00:37:06,592 --> 00:37:08,219
- It's thick.
- Right. Sure.

453
00:37:08,302 --> 00:37:10,388
I'll take this in all colors.

454
00:37:10,722 --> 00:37:11,848
On top of that

455
00:37:12,974 --> 00:37:15,685
I ended up in our CEO's arms
on my first day.

456
00:37:15,768 --> 00:37:16,811
What?

457
00:37:19,021 --> 00:37:20,481
What kind
of crazy development is this?

458
00:37:22,650 --> 00:37:25,111
I'm done for!

459
00:37:35,246 --> 00:37:39,167
So the one
who slammed her face into your chest

460
00:37:39,250 --> 00:37:40,334
was Ms. Nam Da-reum?

461
00:37:41,669 --> 00:37:45,298
She's from SE Corporation
of all places.

462
00:37:45,590 --> 00:37:46,883
Something doesn't feel right.

463
00:37:47,383 --> 00:37:49,552
If she had put it on her resume,
I wouldn't have hired her.

464
00:37:49,635 --> 00:37:50,928
COMPUTER SKILLS LEVEL 1,
SURVEY ANALYST LEVEL 2...

465
00:37:51,429 --> 00:37:53,806
I don't see a reason
why she wants to work at Appello.

466
00:37:56,851 --> 00:37:58,603
Mr. Kang, do you think

467
00:37:58,811 --> 00:38:01,022
she could be a corporate spy
working with Director Kim?

468
00:38:02,273 --> 00:38:04,108
I looked into it and found out that

469
00:38:04,192 --> 00:38:07,445
he has infiltrated a few businesses
with spies to take them over.

470
00:38:10,364 --> 00:38:12,825
Let's keep
a close eye on her for a while.

471
00:38:27,423 --> 00:38:29,258
In a way, Appello is quite smart.

472
00:38:29,634 --> 00:38:32,011
Everyone is busy
trying to snatch famous designers

473
00:38:32,094 --> 00:38:33,638
but you're going after new ones.

474
00:38:34,847 --> 00:38:36,098
It was Director Lee's idea.

475
00:38:36,557 --> 00:38:38,059
He was sad to see
talented brands disappear

476
00:38:38,142 --> 00:38:40,895
due to their lack of network
in distribution.

477
00:38:40,978 --> 00:38:43,064
Have you two always known each other?

478
00:38:43,356 --> 00:38:44,524
We went to high school together.

479
00:38:44,732 --> 00:38:46,442
Oh, you two must be best friends.

480
00:38:47,360 --> 00:38:48,861
That's why
he left the business with you.

481
00:38:57,829 --> 00:39:00,039
Goodness. I look forward
to working with you.

482
00:39:00,122 --> 00:39:02,875
SE Corporation is now taking part
in the e-commerce industry.

483
00:39:03,125 --> 00:39:05,461
We plan to open up
a fashion platform very soon.

484
00:39:05,753 --> 00:39:08,798
Wait, does that mean
you're competing against Appello?

485
00:39:09,465 --> 00:39:11,175
Compete? Hardly.

486
00:39:11,676 --> 00:39:13,469
We need to be similar in size
for that to happen.

487
00:39:14,595 --> 00:39:17,098
Wouldn't it be weirder
if we fail to lead the market

488
00:39:17,181 --> 00:39:19,684
with our resources
and distribution network?

489
00:39:24,689 --> 00:39:28,025
So you used investment as an excuse
to get our intel, in case you fail.

490
00:39:28,734 --> 00:39:31,696
I heard you've done that
with a few businesses with spies.

491
00:39:32,405 --> 00:39:33,614
Spies?

492
00:39:35,241 --> 00:39:36,909
Then what about Appello?

493
00:39:37,451 --> 00:39:40,371
Do you think one of my people
is there or not?

494
00:40:21,996 --> 00:40:23,581
CEO Kang Ha-gi?

495
00:40:25,082 --> 00:40:27,376
I am Reporter Do Eun-yong
with Insight Business Newspaper.

496
00:40:28,920 --> 00:40:30,671
INSIGHT BUSINESS NEWSPAPER
REPORTER DO EUN-YONG

497
00:40:31,172 --> 00:40:33,799
Nice to meet you. I look forward
to seeing great articles about us.

498
00:40:38,054 --> 00:40:41,265
Why don't you spare me some time?
I have many questions for you.

499
00:40:41,891 --> 00:40:43,893
Please contact my office
to schedule an interview.

500
00:40:43,976 --> 00:40:44,977
I don't mean Appello.

501
00:40:45,728 --> 00:40:46,771
I mean for you.

502
00:40:55,071 --> 00:40:56,948
I'm almost there. See you soon.

503
00:40:57,031 --> 00:40:58,491
I'm sorry. I must be somewhere.

504
00:41:00,451 --> 00:41:01,452
Are you done?

505
00:41:18,344 --> 00:41:19,971
Why are you so dressed up?

506
00:41:20,638 --> 00:41:22,181
You're wearing perfume too.

507
00:41:22,515 --> 00:41:23,975
Stop getting clingy.

508
00:41:24,058 --> 00:41:26,727
Why? It's been so long
since we've met.

509
00:41:29,313 --> 00:41:30,606
You only call me for business.

510
00:41:31,440 --> 00:41:33,651
Why are you staying at a hotel
and not at your place?

511
00:41:34,276 --> 00:41:35,403
Someone kept visiting me.

512
00:41:37,405 --> 00:41:39,740
Be careful.
That can turn into an owner's risk.

513
00:41:40,116 --> 00:41:41,575
We're over already

514
00:41:41,784 --> 00:41:42,827
and it was an industry insider.

515
00:41:43,619 --> 00:41:45,121
You'd better keep that up.

516
00:41:46,956 --> 00:41:49,125
Only date someone
who has something to lose.

517
00:41:52,128 --> 00:41:55,214
