Use that glass.

630
00:49:33,755 --> 00:49:35,424
Right. Yes, sir!

631
00:49:36,300 --> 00:49:37,301
Okay.

632
00:49:38,635 --> 00:49:39,636
What?

633
00:49:43,348 --> 00:49:44,349
Team dinners are voluntary.

634
00:49:45,642 --> 00:49:46,935
If you're exhausted, you may go home.

635
00:49:49,646 --> 00:49:51,565
Yes, sir. I will.

636
00:50:18,967 --> 00:50:20,969
MEAT BARBECUE

637
00:50:22,846 --> 00:50:27,267
I should go for a quick recharge.

638
00:50:30,562 --> 00:50:32,439
- Drink up!
- Cheers!

639
00:50:33,857 --> 00:50:35,943
- Cheers!
- Have another drink.

640
00:50:36,360 --> 00:50:38,320
I have to be at a meeting soon,
so please excuse me.

641
00:50:38,612 --> 00:50:40,531
Yes, you should get going, Mr. Kang.

642
00:50:41,406 --> 00:50:43,116
Goodbye, Mr. Kang.

643
00:50:46,620 --> 00:50:47,704
Oh, okay.

644
00:50:49,748 --> 00:50:52,084
- I need some more.
- Come on!

645
00:51:04,429 --> 00:51:05,722
Why is Director Kim here?

646
00:51:19,319 --> 00:51:20,988
Darn it.

647
00:51:55,772 --> 00:51:59,109
If I work hard enough

648
00:51:59,610 --> 00:52:00,777
then one day

649
00:52:03,363 --> 00:52:06,825
I'll get to see you in person, right?

650
00:52:13,206 --> 00:52:16,752
Anyway, he looks really good
in this picture.

651
00:52:18,629 --> 00:52:21,465
I must take a picture.

652
00:52:27,638 --> 00:52:28,889
PASSCODE

653
00:52:29,848 --> 00:52:31,308
Why isn't it working?

654
00:52:32,309 --> 00:52:35,312
Zero. Nine. One. Six.

655
00:52:38,315 --> 00:52:40,942
That's Chan's birthday.

656
00:52:41,610 --> 00:52:45,906
Zero. Nine. One...

657
00:52:57,084 --> 00:52:58,085
Ms. Nam.

658
00:52:58,877 --> 00:52:59,920
Yes?

659
00:53:01,129 --> 00:53:02,673
What do you think you're doing here?

660
00:53:04,549 --> 00:53:05,676
Mr. Kang?

661
00:53:05,759 --> 00:53:07,344
Why are you here
in the middle of a company dinner?

662
00:53:07,761 --> 00:53:08,762
What?

663
00:53:09,221 --> 00:53:10,681
Me? You mean me?

664
00:53:11,223 --> 00:53:13,392
Oh, I...

665
00:53:13,600 --> 00:53:16,436
I needed to recharge for a bit.

666
00:53:17,104 --> 00:53:20,023
- Recharge?
- You said you always

667
00:53:21,066 --> 00:53:22,776
welcomed everyone

668
00:53:22,859 --> 00:53:24,361
and that your office

669
00:53:25,278 --> 00:53:27,656
was always open.

670
00:53:28,615 --> 00:53:31,410
So a picture.

671
00:53:32,035 --> 00:53:36,915
I was going to leave
after taking just one picture.

672
00:53:38,709 --> 00:53:39,710
What picture?

673
00:53:40,460 --> 00:53:41,461
A picture...

674
00:53:55,308 --> 00:53:58,145
Now, everyone. Attention, please.

675
00:53:58,937 --> 00:54:02,399
There is one question all rookies
of our company must answer.

676
00:54:02,482 --> 00:54:03,567
Yes, that one.

677
00:54:03,650 --> 00:54:06,153
Now, dear adorable Ms. Lee Min-a

678
00:54:06,236 --> 00:54:09,990
are you on Team Ha-gi or Team Chan?

679
00:54:11,074 --> 00:54:13,118
- What?
- Do you prefer someone like Mr. Kang

680
00:54:13,201 --> 00:54:14,828
who's very trustworthy

681
00:54:14,911 --> 00:54:16,747
and hard on the outside,
but soft on the inside?

682
00:54:16,830 --> 00:54:18,331
Or is it Director Chan

683
00:54:18,415 --> 00:54:20,500
someone unreal,
like he popped out of a fairy tale?

684
00:54:21,626 --> 00:54:23,670
Well, the thing is

685
00:54:23,754 --> 00:54:25,922
there's too much pressure.

686
00:54:26,006 --> 00:54:29,384
If they're too much pressure for you,
you can join Team Jin-sang.

687
00:54:30,010 --> 00:54:31,553
- Join me.
- What?

688
00:54:32,471 --> 00:54:34,347
- What?
- Come on. You ruined it.

689
00:54:34,431 --> 00:54:35,724
Hurry up and choose.

690
00:54:35,807 --> 00:54:37,726
In that case, I choose...

691
00:54:43,899 --> 00:54:46,193
Team Ha-gi.

692
00:54:47,569 --> 00:54:49,112
- I knew it.
- I was right.

693
00:54:49,196 --> 00:54:50,447
See? Me too.

694
00:54:50,530 --> 00:54:52,157
- Nice choice, Min-a.
- I was right.

695
00:54:52,240 --> 00:54:53,492
- I had a feeling.
- I'm on Team Ha-gi too!

696
00:54:53,575 --> 00:54:55,410
Why is everyone on Team Ha-gi?

697
00:54:55,494 --> 00:54:57,662
- Is anybody on Team Jin-sang?
- It's Ha-gi.

698
00:55:22,646 --> 00:55:25,232
Did she really break in
because she was just drunk?

699
00:56:40,056 --> 00:56:41,349
She didn't hear that, did she?

700
00:56:47,772 --> 00:56:48,773
Ms. Nam.

701
00:57:02,537 --> 00:57:04,080
Ms. Nam, time to go home.

702
00:57:04,748 --> 00:57:06,291
Wake up, Ms. Nam.

703
00:57:08,043 --> 00:57:10,211
What? Why?

704
00:57:22,724 --> 00:57:24,643
She's driving me insane.

705
00:57:26,895 --> 00:57:28,104
What now?

706
00:58:04,724 --> 00:58:05,892
I must be insane.

707
00:58:08,228 --> 00:58:09,562
I must be.

708
00:58:11,314 --> 00:58:12,649
Yes, I am.

709
00:58:16,403 --> 00:58:17,821
Oh, come on.

710
00:58:23,243 --> 00:58:24,703
I feel like throwing up.

711
00:58:35,005 --> 00:58:37,465
What? You did it with the CEO...

712
00:58:41,678 --> 00:58:45,640
- You slept with him?
- What? No!

713
00:58:45,724 --> 00:58:49,102
I fell asleep in his office.

714
00:58:52,772 --> 00:58:54,983
I knew it. There's no way
our conservative girl would do that.

715
00:58:55,775 --> 00:58:57,235
So why did you go there?

716
00:58:59,571 --> 00:59:00,697
No idea.

717
00:59:01,197 --> 00:59:02,699
I guess
I was in my zombie mode again.

718
00:59:03,491 --> 00:59:05,410
There's a picture of Chan there.

719
00:59:05,493 --> 00:59:08,830
It's not a photoshoot, though.
It's such a candid picture.

720
00:59:08,913 --> 00:59:10,081
You're insane.

721
00:59:11,624 --> 00:59:13,626
You have to do something
about your drunken behavior.

722
00:59:13,710 --> 00:59:16,046
Da-reum,
you literally are killing me.

723
00:59:16,796 --> 00:59:20,050
I'm sorry.
I'll seriously quit drinking now.

724
00:59:20,383 --> 00:59:21,384
Jeez!

725
00:59:24,971 --> 00:59:27,474
Anyway, you didn't do
anything weird in the office, right?

726
00:59:27,974 --> 00:59:28,975
I

727
00:59:29,726 --> 00:59:30,977
hope not.

728
00:59:33,313 --> 00:59:35,106
What is this ominous feeling?

729
00:59:35,190 --> 00:59:37,192
- I don't know.
- Wait, no.

730
00:59:38,735 --> 00:59:39,861
Did you black out?

731
00:59:40,945 --> 00:59:41,988
Yes.

732
00:59:46,367 --> 00:59:47,702
Hey, Da-reum.

733
00:59:47,786 --> 00:59:50,288
- Hello.
- Oh, hello.

734
01:00:03,760 --> 01:00:05,970
Hey, Nam Da-reum!

735
01:00:06,971 --> 01:00:08,598
I saw a new side of you yesterday.

736
01:00:08,681 --> 01:00:10,809
You did something with this thing

737
01:00:10,892 --> 01:00:15,063
and bang, the bottle cap spun around,
flew over there, and blast!

738
01:00:16,731 --> 01:00:18,191
Gosh, you truly are different.

739
01:00:18,942 --> 01:00:20,360
- Give me five.
- What?

740
01:00:21,402 --> 01:00:24,280
M-Me? What did I do? Why...

741
01:00:27,075 --> 01:00:28,076
What's going on?

742
01:00:29,244 --> 01:00:31,037
You were so cool yesterday, Da-reum.

743
01:00:31,121 --> 01:00:32,288
You're the best, Da-reum.

744
01:00:43,967 --> 01:00:46,386
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

745
01:00:51,808 --> 01:00:52,934
- Da-reum.
- Yes?

746
01:00:53,017 --> 01:00:54,394
Did you get home safely last night?

747
01:00:54,602 --> 01:00:56,146
You seemed to have left
after getting drunk.

748
01:00:56,396 --> 01:00:57,939
Yes, I did.

749
01:01:06,114 --> 01:01:08,700
He's so good-looking.

750
01:01:08,783 --> 01:01:11,202
Ms. Nam.

751
01:01:12,579 --> 01:01:14,706
Wait, what is this memory?

752
01:01:15,248 --> 01:01:16,916
It feels like Mr. Kang was there.

753
01:01:18,126 --> 01:01:20,253
- Excuse me, Ms. Kim.
- Yes?

754
01:01:20,336 --> 01:01:23,590
By any chance, is Mr. Kang at work?

755
01:01:23,673 --> 01:01:24,757
Mr. Kang?

756
01:01:25,008 --> 01:01:26,801
I think
he spent the night up in his office.

757
01:01:27,177 --> 01:01:28,178
What?

758
01:01:35,977 --> 01:01:37,687
Darn it. What's going on?

759
01:01:37,896 --> 01:01:39,981
What happened?
Why is he looking at me?

760
01:01:40,315 --> 01:01:43,818
Please recall it.
Think hard, Nam Da-reum.

761
01:01:44,194 --> 01:01:46,279
SAMPLE ROOM

762
01:01:58,374 --> 01:02:00,376
I don't think I've sobered up yet.

763
01:02:00,835 --> 01:02:03,296
Da-reum! You were here?

764
01:02:03,630 --> 01:02:05,381
- Do you feel okay?
- Yes.

765
01:02:06,633 --> 01:02:08,509
I got wasted last night, wasn't I?

766
01:02:08,801 --> 01:02:10,887
Did I make any mistakes?

767
01:02:10,970 --> 01:02:13,223
Mistakes? What mistakes?

768
01:02:13,306 --> 01:02:15,016
You left early,
so you didn't have time to do that.

769
01:02:15,099 --> 01:02:19,479
Da-reum, it would've been so much fun
if you stayed until the very end.

770
01:02:19,562 --> 01:02:22,398
At the end of the night,
Director Lee Chan came!

771
01:02:22,482 --> 01:02:24,108
He was so good-looking.

772
01:02:25,068 --> 01:02:26,110
What?

773
01:02:26,986 --> 01:02:28,112
My goodness.

774
01:02:28,196 --> 01:02:31,532
I thought he was just good-looking,
but he was hilarious too.

775
01:02:31,616 --> 01:02:32,825
- Yes.
- See?

776
01:02:32,909 --> 01:02:35,578
He only took a picture with us
to congratulate us on our start here!

777
01:02:40,333 --> 01:02:41,751
My Chan was there?

778
01:02:43,670 --> 01:02:48,007
You should call him
Director Lee at work.

779
01:02:48,091 --> 01:02:51,052
Shouldn't we call him that?

780
01:02:51,886 --> 01:02:55,181
Wait, Da-reum must've been
a fan of D.N.X.

781
01:02:55,473 --> 01:02:57,100
I almost said, "It's Lee Chan!"

782
01:02:57,809 --> 01:02:58,851
It could've been a mistake.

783
01:02:59,269 --> 01:03:00,270
Oh, no.

784
01:03:01,187 --> 01:03:02,689
What's wrong, Da-reum?

785
01:03:03,481 --> 01:03:05,024
Was it something I said?

786
01:03:08,486 --> 01:03:09,654
It's not that.

787
01:03:11,155 --> 01:03:12,282
It's nothing.

788
01:03:23,334 --> 01:03:24,711
Not only was I drunk

789
01:03:26,087 --> 01:03:28,256
but I broke into the CEO's office

790
01:03:30,800 --> 01:03:32,385
and didn't even get to see my Chan.

791
01:03:38,349 --> 01:03:40,268
Why are you even alive, Da-reum?

792
01:03:41,644 --> 01:03:43,479
Just end yourself.

793
01:03:45,815 --> 01:03:48,735
That was my chance
to finally see him in person.

794
01:04:33,279 --> 01:04:34,280
Oh, mother!

795
01:04:37,658 --> 01:04:40,078
Why do you always look for your mom
whenever you see me?

796
01:04:41,496 --> 01:04:43,247
So, about yesterday...

797
01:04:46,000 --> 01:04:47,251
I'm sorry, Mr. Kang.

798
01:04:47,919 --> 01:04:50,963
I remember getting drunk
and walking into your office.

799
01:04:51,506 --> 01:04:53,549
But when I opened my eyes,
it was already morning.

800
01:04:56,928 --> 01:04:58,012
So you don't remember?

801
01:04:59,597 --> 01:05:01,849
How convenient.
You never remember anything.

802
01:05:03,184 --> 01:05:04,727
- Sorry?
- Forget it.

803
01:05:05,478 --> 01:05:06,604
It's better that way.

804
01:05:07,814 --> 01:05:09,148
I wanted to wake you
when you sobered up.

805
01:05:09,232 --> 01:05:11,234
But you were too drunk to do that.

806
01:05:11,526 --> 01:05:14,278
Then what about you?

807
01:05:17,448 --> 01:05:18,449
Well...

808
01:05:21,494 --> 01:05:22,495
I worked and left.

809
01:05:25,123 --> 01:05:27,250
Yes, right? I'm glad.

810
01:05:27,708 --> 01:05:29,085
I'm glad you didn't stay
because of me.

811
01:05:29,168 --> 01:05:30,294
Please be cautious from now on.

812
01:05:30,378 --> 01:05:31,421
That kind of behavior

813
01:05:32,255 --> 01:05:33,881
may cause
an unnecessary misunderstanding.

814
01:05:35,591 --> 01:05:36,592
Yes, sir.

815
01:05:37,009 --> 01:05:38,219
I'm sorry, Mr. Kang.

816
01:05:38,553 --> 01:05:40,263
I won't let
anything like this happen again.

817
01:05:42,306 --> 01:05:43,307
I'm sorry.

818
01:05:47,728 --> 01:05:49,272
- Yes, Ms. Kim.
- Hey, Da-reum.

819
01:05:49,355 --> 01:05:52,108
Go to the showroom on the first floor
and help out with organizing.

820
01:05:52,191 --> 01:05:53,401
Yes, coming.

821
01:05:55,027 --> 01:05:57,196
Ms. Kim needs me at the showroom

822
01:05:57,280 --> 01:05:58,990
so please excuse me.

823
01:06:08,791 --> 01:06:09,917
Ms. Nam.

824
01:06:14,505 --> 01:06:15,756
What? Why is he following me?

825
01:06:28,895 --> 01:06:31,272
The miracle I had always hoped for

826
01:06:33,149 --> 01:06:34,984
did not happen on a special day.

827
01:06:37,069 --> 01:06:39,947
It came into my trivial daily life

828
01:06:42,617 --> 01:06:45,578
in the least expected moment.

829
01:07:20,112 --> 01:07:23,699
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

830
01:07:34,752 --> 01:07:36,087
CHEON SEON-AE

831
01:07:36,170 --> 01:07:37,713
EPILOGUE

832
01:08:22,174 --> 01:08:24,677
Scrub with love

833
01:08:24,760 --> 01:08:28,180
Scrub the dirt off your heart

834
01:08:28,723 --> 01:08:32,101
Every corner, every grime

835
01:08:32,184 --> 01:08:34,729
Let me scrub it off for you

836
01:08:35,730 --> 01:08:39,609
Scrub, scrub with love

837
01:08:39,692 --> 01:08:43,029
The dirt on the bruise of your heart

838
01:08:43,279 --> 01:08:46,324
I will even scrub the bruises

839
01:08:46,699 --> 01:08:52,079
Of your heart with my love

840
01:08:52,163 --> 01:08:53,539
Scrub, scrub

841
01:08:53,956 --> 01:08:55,541
- Oh, my. Mr. Kang.
- Goodness.

842
01:08:56,500 --> 01:08:59,253
I mean,
it's a good morning, Ms. Cheon.

843
01:08:59,337 --> 01:09:01,339
Oh, no.
Did you spend the night up again?

844
01:09:01,422 --> 01:09:02,757
You should take a quick nap.

845
01:09:02,840 --> 01:09:04,467
I'll clean up quickly and leave.

846
01:09:09,430 --> 01:09:11,891
No, it's all right.

847
01:09:11,974 --> 01:09:13,309
My paperwork is all over the place.

848
01:09:13,392 --> 01:09:15,686
That's nothing new.

849
01:09:15,770 --> 01:09:17,605
It's not like
I've ever touched anything.

850
01:09:17,688 --> 01:09:19,565
If you have work to do, go ahead.

851
01:09:19,649 --> 01:09:21,108
I'll make it quick and leave.

852
01:09:23,903 --> 01:09:25,738
Ms. Cheon.

853
01:09:27,114 --> 01:09:28,866
Dear Ms. Cheon.

854
01:09:30,493 --> 01:09:31,494
Would you like

855
01:09:32,453 --> 01:09:33,746
to have a cup of coffee with me?

856
01:09:34,622 --> 01:09:37,792
Coffee? Morning coffee sounds great.

857
01:09:38,709 --> 01:09:42,213
Scrub, scrub, scrub the dirt

858
01:09:49,261 --> 01:09:51,347
- Nice to meet you, Da-reum.
- How do you know my name?

859
01:09:51,597 --> 01:09:52,932
I'm not dreaming, am I?

860
01:09:53,766 --> 01:09:55,434
Overseas training
for outstanding employees?

861
01:09:56,310 --> 01:09:58,562
I feel like she has a hidden agenda.

862
01:09:58,646 --> 01:10:00,648
Mr. Kang.

863
01:10:00,731 --> 01:10:02,608
You look so cool today.

864
01:10:02,983 --> 01:10:05,027
Maybe she's a honey trap

865
01:10:05,736 --> 01:10:06,862
Director Kim sent.

866
01:10:07,113 --> 01:10:09,365
- Call me.
- See you again!

867
01:10:10,866 --> 01:10:11,951
They're dating?

868
01:10:12,034 --> 01:10:13,869
Our company CEO and Chan?

869
01:10:13,953 --> 01:10:16,997
No!

